<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-02-the-bathroom" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Bathroom</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      We now expand beyond handwashing and look at the bathroom as a whole.
      In <xref ref="ch-01-handwashing"/>, we treated the skin simply as a surface with an oil layer and dirt particles to be cleaned.
      But to truly understand how our bathroom products work, we have to treat the skin as more than a surface and gain a deeper understanding of our bodies.
    </p>

    <p>
      A major theme in this chapter will be the <term>integumentary system</term> <mdash/> a fancy term for the parts of our bodies that reside on its surface, such as the skin, hair, and nails.
      We will be exploring their structures and how chemicals interact with them on a molecular level.
    </p>
  </introduction>
